# =========================================================================================== #
# File: '.gitignore'
# --- [ Description ] ----------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
# DEFAULT-DENY, EXPLICIT INCLUDES ONLY. Nothing in this working tree is tracked unless it is
# allowed below, by name. Publishing a file is therefore a deliberate act rather than an
# accident -- see docs/decision-records/org/0003-use-deny-all-gitignore-strategy.md.
#
# Entries are ROOTED with a leading '/' so an allow means one path, not every path that happens
# to end the same way. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so every directory on
# the way to an allowed file is re-included by name; those directory lines publish nothing by
# themselves.
#
# =========================================================================================== #

# --- [ ignore everything ] ------------------------------------------------------------------ #
**

# --- [ allowed: the allowlist and normalization rules ] ------------------------------------- #
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# --- [ allowed: repository configuration ] -------------------------------------------------- #
!/pyproject.toml
!/uv.lock
!/.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
!/.pre-commit-config.yaml

# --- [ allowed: top-level documents ] ------------------------------------------------------- #
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CHANGELOG.md

# --- [ allowed: GitHub and editor configuration ] ------------------------------------------- #
!/.github/
!/.github/**
!/.vscode/
!/.vscode/**

# --- [ allowed: the shared quality-gate tools ] --------------------------------------------- #
# Synced from the type-template; never hand-edited here.
!/tools/
!/tools/**

# --- [ allowed: source and tests ] ---------------------------------------------------------- #
# The product modules live under src/software_update_publisher/products/<product>/. They are
# allowed by this same spine: a module is a normal package, so adding one adds no allowlist
# line. What a module may NOT publish is covered by the artifact rules at the end of this file,
# so a stray capture, download or credential inside a product folder stays ignored.
!/src/
!/src/**
!/tests/
!/tests/**

# --- [ allowed: documentation ] ------------------------------------------------------------- #
!/docs/
!/docs/**

# --- [ never tracked, even inside an allowed directory ] ------------------------------------ #
# Build and tool output.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/.mypy_cache/
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/coverage.xml
/htmlcov/

# Acquired artifacts. This repository downloads vendor installers; none of them belong in git.
*.msi
*.exe
*.cab
*.zip
*.nupkg
*.tar.gz
*.rpm
*.msu

# Anything that could carry a credential or a live account identifier.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
